      "side": 0,
      "message": "Thanks for explanation and pointer to bug.  Your explanation makes complete sense now that I\u0027ve re-read this part of spec in particular,\n\nIf a single message represents both a transition to HPD_High and an IRQ_HPD, the converter\nshall ensure that HPD is taken high for a minimum of 2ms before generating the IRQ_HPD.\n\nMeaning its perfectly reasonable for HPD-\u003ePD transmitter to group both the original HPD assertion and its first IRQ together and for that reason cur_lvl could be low.\n\nI think previously, we saw packets where at least the initial HPD was asserted in the absence of the IRQ always.",
